# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN A WORKING SITE AND A BROKEN ONE.
#
# The app is a single-page React Router build: only `/index.html` physically
# exists. Every other route — /about, /contact, /programs, /rules, /faq,
# /how-convex-works, /legal/* — is created by JavaScript after index.html loads.
#
# Without this rule a static host looks for a real file at those paths, does not
# find one, and returns 404. That is fine while you click around inside the app,
# because the router never asks the server. It breaks the moment anyone hard
# refreshes, opens a link in a new tab, or arrives from a shared URL — which is
# every legal link in the footer.
#
# Measured before this file existed, serving dist/ with a plain static server:
#   /                  200
#   /contact           404
#   /legal/terms       404
#   /legal/privacy     404
#   /legal/risk        404
#
# The 200 (not 302) is what matters: it serves index.html AT the requested URL
# rather than redirecting, so the router still sees /contact and renders the
# right page, and search engines see a real page rather than a redirect chain.
#
# Real files always win over this rule, so /sequence-desktop/frame_000.webp and
# /assets/* are unaffected.

/*    /index.html   200
